The Java robot simulator sends a completion event when it reaches the pick waypoint, even if the gripper is still open. The gripper command is asynchronous, so the delayed-grip fixture reports “completion observed with gripper open.” The fixture already exposes `robot`, `gripper`, and `completed` fields. Add this exact test method to that fixture:
```java
@Test
void waitsForGrip() {
    gripper.holdOpen();
    robot.startPick();
    robot.advanceToWaypoint();
    assertFalse(completed.get());
    gripper.confirmClosed();
    assertTrue(completed.get());
}
```
This method is the proposed regression code to paste, using the fixture’s existing control points. The controller’s observable completion must depend on both motion and grip state, while cancellation remains available.

